# Brainstorm and project selection

### Initial ideas explored:
- Building defect classification
- Satellite land-cover classification
- Post-disaster building damage classification
- Sports sponsorship exposure
- Plant disease detection
  - The plant-disease idea was refined into grapevine disease classification. The current GVLiD dataset contains field-acquired images in four classes: healthy, black rot, esca and leaf blight.

The group selected this option because it combined business relevance, local context, a clear image-classification problem and a manageable dataset.

### Final concept
Use a CNN to classify visible grapevine diseases and support growers in identifying vines that may require expert inspection or treatment.

### Future extensions discussed 
Data augmentation, transfer learning, confidence thresholds/human review, geospatial disease mapping, temporal monitoring and disease severity estimation.

The team agreed to focus primarily on one CNN model, with alternative architectures discussed conceptually and only tested if time allows.
